istanbul is turkey's biggest city and  main economic hub many large firms are  based here under erdogan's rule turkey  has been transformed from a country in  economic crisis to regional power  after he became prime minister in 2003  erdogan privatized large state-owned  companies including the oil and gas  industry ports and airports and  liberalized the labor market hundreds of  new companies were created turkey also  recovered surprisingly quickly from the  global financial crisis the turkish  economy has grown in recent years by an  average of five percent annually  but not everyone here is thrilled about  erdogan's victory  critics fear the new president could  exert greater influence than before on  the economy  and  on the central bank  erdogan's drive to cut interest rates  and weaken turkey's currency has  undermined the credibility of its  monetary authorities and it has also  deterred investors  and while the economy remains strong the  lira is falling for years turkey has  imported more goods than it exports and  has been piling up debt
 

